@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: a finished headless run's report reads in the right pane; its file:line references open the file there
' covers: internal/dashboard/report.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/report_test.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/data.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/cards.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/model.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/view.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/filetree.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/highlight.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/handoff_test.go
' covers: go.mod
' covers: internal/dashboard/mouse.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/mouse_test.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/popover_test.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/links.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/links_test.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/popover.go
' covers: internal/dashboard/review.go
'
' "the review finished but it exited the sandbox; i cannot attach to see the
' results. Now, sbx can output reports, perhaps this is what the sbx community
' intends to happen. Judge this flow and recommend." (2026-11-26)
' RESEARCHED 2026-11-26: sbx collects no output. Its schedules page: "Instruct
' the task to save results to an external destination before it exits"; a
' run's inspect shows state, exit code and timing only; its CI page fetches
' the clone's commits and removes the sandbox. Proveo already does what sbx
' asks: a plain run's report moves next to its transcript
' (~/.proveo/logs/schedule/<job>/<stamp>.report.md) and Result.Report names it.
' The gap was the dashboard: it never read Result.Report, so attach was the
' only way in, and attach ends with the run.
' CHOSEN: "↵ report, s follow up" and "glamour in-pane".
' CARD: an ended run with a report leads with ↵ report, then s follow up (the
' resume of ended-runs.puml), r retry, x clean up.
' PANE: ↵ swaps the task cards for the report, rendered by glamour v2
' (charm.land/glamour/v2) at the pane's width: identity colours for text,
' headings, links and inline code; fenced code takes the chroma theme code
' previews take (PROVEO_CODE_THEME), the palette's one exception.
' REFERENCES: every `path:line` code span and every local image is a
' reference. Before rendering, each gets an invisible marker (U+2063, its
' index in U+2061/U+2062 binary, U+2063); the row a marker lands on is the
' reference's row, then the markers go. Substring search failed: tables wrap
' a cell's path across rows. n p walk them top to bottom; the selected row
' gets ›; ↵ opens the file in the tree (exact path, else the first path
' ending with it) at that line, marked N›; Esc from the file returns to the
' report. A path outside the tree says "f lists every file".
' IMAGES: Alacritty has no image protocol (alacritty#4763 open since 2021),
' so local PNG, JPEG and GIF draw as half-block thumbnails (charmbracelet/x/
' mosaic, 60 cells by 18 rows at most) under their line; o or ↵ hands the
' full image to the OS viewer (open on macOS, xdg-open on Linux). o with no
' image selected opens the report file itself.
' MEASURED 2026-11-26: review #3951's report gave 16 references and #3995's 23,
' each on its own row, tables included.
' COPY (2026-11-27, "the Markdown renderer does not allow cursor highlight to
' copy/paste"; chosen "In-pane selection + y"): the dashboard reports the mouse
' (cell motion), so Alacritty selects only with Shift, across both panes, and
' copies inline code's no-break spaces. A drag over the report marks whole
' rows (▌ and the surface colour) and its release copies them; a click alone
' copies nothing. v marks the row under › (else the top row), ↑↓ extend, y
' copies, Esc clears first and closes second. y with no selection copies the
' selected path:line; Y copies the report's Markdown source. Copied text has
' no gutter, no SGR, plain spaces and the rows' common indent removed. It goes
' out as OSC 52 (tea.SetClipboard) and through pbcopy on macOS, else wl-copy or
' xclip, so a terminal without OSC 52 still gets it.
' WHEEL (2026-11-27, "The mouse wheel seems to move the file-tree while the right
' pane (file/report) is highlighted"): the wheel followed the keys' focus, and
' over a report it fell through to the task list, whose next task swapped the
' tree. Each draw records both panes' frames; the wheel scrolls the pane under
' the pointer (tree, file, report or tasks), three rows a notch for text, and
' follows the focus only off both panes. A click gives its pane the keys.
' LINKS (2026-11-27, "Can links be copied to the clipboard when clicking on them?
' e.g. in Task Details"): a click never reached the terminal's OSC 8 handling,
' since the dashboard reports the mouse. Each draw scans its finished frame for
' OSC 8 spans (ansi.DecodeSequence: the cells each covers and its target), so
' Task Details links, card PR links, the plan and every glamour link count;
' glamour links a wrapped address on every row with the whole URL. A left
' click on a span copies the target (a file: link copies its path) before any
' focus or selection; Task Details then says "click a link copies it".
' CARD NUMBERS (2026-11-27, "Let the PR numbers e.g. #3951 become links in each card;
' let a tooltip display for 2.4s with copied to clipboard"): a ghost's #N links
' its PR; a task card's ticket label (#3995 from a PR or issue address, or a
' Linear id with its issue's address) links its ticket; PR chips already did.
' Every copy that lands raises a small card, ✓ Copied to clipboard, for 2.4 s
' (tooltipFor): above the pointer that clicked or dragged, below it at the top
' edge, at the right pane's foot for y and Y. A newer copy replaces it and its
' own timer; the older timer leaves it. The footer still names what was copied.
' Links look the same everywhere: brand cyan, underlined (tui-design-language).
title Run reports — read the result, jump to its lines

participant "ended card\n↵ report" as CARD <<app>>
participant "report pane\nglamour · markers" as PANE <<app>>
participant "file preview\nN› at the line" as FILE <<app>>
participant "OS viewer\nopen · xdg-open" as OS <<host>>

CARD -> PANE : ↵ (Result.Report)
PANE -> PANE : n p select a reference
PANE -> FILE : ↵ on path:line
FILE --> PANE : Esc
PANE -> OS : o, or ↵ on an image
PANE --> CARD : Esc

note over PANE
  **The report is the result.**
  sbx deletes the sandbox; the report
  stays on the host, so reading it
  needs no session.
end note

note over FILE
  **A finding points at code.**
  ↵ opens the PR's file at the line
  the finding names, so the reviewer
  checks it beside the verdict.
end note
@enduml
